\f1\fs22 This time, Haloren Smythe struck flawlessly. His three-sided stainless-steel spike, the Point of Order, opened a fine, pulsing spray of oxygen-rich blood. He threw his head back and soaked in it, imparadising his chest, chin, and hair.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 When his victim finally went limp from insanguination and Halo\'92s pulse receded, he rose and began the familiar routine of cleaning up. The ritual was calming, a time for reflection as he came back to his more mundane self. Only in these slow, careful minutes could he truly savour his deeds. The work left him refreshed, delivered beyond the chaos of his own appetite. He\'92d survived, maybe even thrived.\
Except he was thriving less with every attack. Later, in the bar, he found himself surveying possible marks, fantasising about his next conquest. The intervals between strikes grew ever shorter, the pleasure of each kill, duller. Except the last one. Maybe it was her resistance. Maybe the extra danger, the flatmate due back any minute. \
Yet already, too soon after conquest, he was flipping through news feeds on his tablet, searching for something that might assuage his thirst, and found:
\f2\fs18 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\ri-1980\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 THE ULYSSIA MORNING SMEAR\
SCARLET SHOWER SURGEON STRIKES AGAIN!\
By Tracey Krullo \'96 Crime Desk\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\ri-1620\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 City residents awoke in fear yesterday as authorities confirmed another victim of the so-called \'93Scarlet Shower Surgeon,\'94 the serial killer whose grisly precision has left experts and police in a spin.\
The latest body bore the telltale mark of the Surgeon\'92s work: a single, perfectly placed puncture just below the jawline, leaving bedroom walls \'93painted in arterial crimson,\'94 according to a forensics spokesperson who has seen enough splatter to retire twice.\
\'93There\'92s never more than one wound,\'94 said a mouthpiece at this morning\'92s press briefing, \'93but the sheer volume of blood\'85 it\'92s like a Pro Hart installation if he\'92d swapped paint for plasma. Whoever this is, we\'92re dealing with someone who knows their way around an anatomy lab.\'94\
The Surgeon\'97whose three-sided weapon has been called everything from \'93the Red Fountain Pen\'94 to \'93the Steely Dagger\'94\'97has now left a trail of bodies across the Pale. All victims died within seconds and were found naked, still in the throes of unspeakable activities, the killer seemingly vanishing without a trace except for the forensic masterpiece left behind.\
\'93This isn\'92t random,\'94 said one criminal profiler and panic merchant. \'93The whole decrepit city\'92s been turned into an art gallery\'97one where the medium is always scarlet.\'94\
While some media sources speculate the Scarlet Shower Surgeon may be a disaffected hospital orderly or a failed cocktail mixologist (a hypothesis TRAMPS have not ruled out), anonymous insiders whisper of more sinister connections\'97secret societies, surgical cults, and a supposed link to the recent spate of cleaning supply thefts from municipal chemical stores.\

\f3\i City officials urge anyone who spots suspicious behaviour, especially around showers, laundromats, or knitting groups, to contact the Scarlet Hotline immediately. The reward for information stands at 250,000 tax credits and a year\'92s free home hazmat cleanups. Meanwhile, stay safe, and, if you must go out, wear a thick scarf.
\f1\i0\fs22 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
Halo sipped. Leaned back in the booth. Breathed calm into his thumping arteries. He scanned the bar for new targets; none baited his interest. In the oldest, darkest caverns of his heart, there lived but a single idol worthy of his attention.\
Sarah.\
She was the magnetic ultimate. Perhaps, after her, he might even stop. What sweet relief that would be.\
On his tablet, Halo opened the Labrador app (so called for the world\'92s most beloved illness-sniffing puppy), and called up the data it collected of Sarah in those precious seconds at the Stickett Inn: breath, pheromones, a glut of key indicators. Sarah was so far off the charts, Labrador assessed her age against various benchmarks as 8, 12, 19 and 28. One benchmark, clearly confused by the extraordinary data points, put Sarah\'92s age at 226.\
Whatever her age, Sarah was a singularly worthy conquest, both for her organic perfection and her awareness of his tech advantages and augmentations. She\'92d be a challenge indeed. Halo savoured the anticipation. \
The bar\'92s screens were playing Halo\'92s favourite: 
\f4\i Curb Your Individualism
\f1\i0 , a semi-documentary delivering homilies about Cloudborne hopefuls in \'93business.\'94 Spoiler: they always got crushed, just for fun, beneath the single-origin alpaca-wool sock of some Airborne corporate foot. This week: a family cleaning business, awarded a huge contract out of nowhere, only to drown (hilariously, of course) in a mine tailings pond. 
\f4\i C.Y.I.
\f1\i0  was closing fast on 
\f4\i Candid Criminal\'92s
\f1\i0  once dominant popularity, a show Halo privately hoped would end with Alexander Shakti, its preposterous host, facing the ultimate trebuchet slap.\
The dialogue from the show muted. \'93We interrupt normal broadcasting for an address from the CEO,\'94 a journalist-sounding voice said.\
Halo snarled as the flat, faintly alien salamander face of Piotr Dunhilton, freshly appointed Chief Executive Officer of the Airborne Meritocracy of Ulyssia, appeared on every screen in the bar.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 No one foresaw Dunhilton\'92s rise after the early \'93retirement\'94 of the previous CEO. Not even the operatives who facilitated the event believed they would succeed. Less than a year before his ascent as Minister of Defence, Border Walls and Trade, Dunhilton had alienated France by cancelling a multi-billion-dollar toiletries deal in preference for a  gaudy alliance with the Brits and Americans. Months later, both \'93allies\'94 admitted they couldn\'92t supply Ulyssia with so much as a single bar of soap for the next four decades. Unbothered, Dunhilton pledged to fund a soap factory in Adelaide, exploiting the condition of the Murray River, which was already ninety percent suds. But as it way with all promises involving Adelaide and full employment, the dirty deal dissolved in the wash. And so it came to pass that the Airborne meritocrats of Ulyssia were left scrubbing their arses with domestic Cloudborne soap made of cement, ground up coral, and shredded sandpaper.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Nevertheless, Dunhilton was proof positive that, in Ulyssian politics, privilege and corruption would always triumph over competence\'97which shocked precisely nobody. Ulyssia was, after all, a no-liability sovereign state incorporated in Panama, its registered address a recycling wheelie-bin on Kangaroo Island.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 \'93My fellow Airborne Ulyssians,\'94 the salamander face intoned into the mic. \'93When I became CEO of our proud profit-seeking country, I promised decent people everywhere I would scourge all lazy, undeserving minority groups. I also promised to strike out against the immorality of those who expect an even break simply because they exist. I will always fight for true Ulyssians: those who have virtuously inherited, cleverly grifted, or have been righteously awarded their wealth.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 The CEO paused for effect. Halo ground his teeth.\
\'93As I am sure you are aware, Cloudborne agitators have escalated their criminal activities in recent times. You have seen the destruction of property in bomb attacks; and the unlawful violence against government agents who work tirelessly for your security. You may have heard of not-for-profit terrorists who conduct their seditious business, poisoning the simple minds of the once peaceful and compliant, and who are now fomenting disunity in their ghettos and enclaves. Yes, these are troubling times, my fellow Airborne, times when those who are institutionally disentitled agitate for more than they deserve; when those who are worth nothing concoct presumptuous notions of self-worth; when those without connections seek to connect above their stations. Well, let me assure you, I\'92m making it my sacred mission to end all that. I\'92ll hand you over to the new Commissioner of Traffic Movement and Property Security Incorporated.\'94\
A frog-mouthed stubble-cheeked mouthpiece stepped up to the mic. Shuffling in behind him, to bask before the camera\'92s eye, was the preposterous Lieutenant Alexander Shakti. 
\f4\i Lieutenant is not even a real rank in the police force
\f1\i0 , Halo bitterly thought.\
The frog mouth spoke. \'93After intense investigation, and extraordinary collaboration between agencies, we have been able to plot connections between recent nefarious activities: the bombing at the Stickett Inn; civil unrest among the Elvi; industrial espionage against Ulyssia\'92s premier stasis unit authority; and the radicalisation of the public transport sector. All lines lead to a single individual. Yesterday, we apprehended him, and we are assisting him to answer our enquiries.\'94\
\'93Commissioner! Commissioner! Can you identify the perpetrator?\'94 came the chorused squawk of reporters.\
The Commissioner checked with Alexander, who gave his trademark gameshow-host nod.\
\'93Yes, I can,\'94 said the Commissioner. \'93The perpetrator is a small-business pretender, probable unionist, and alleged not-for-profit terrorist named Anthony Chantara.\'94\
Halo nearly spat his beer. \'93Chanta?\'94\
One reporter jumped in: \'93Can you confirm Cloudborne Chantara is being investigated for the disappearance of Airborne Cyber Specialist Sarah Jacobson?\'94\
Now Halo sat up straight, every muscle tensed.\
The Commissioner paused for a word from Alexander. \'93Yes, we believe the perpetrator uses cleaning agents as a form of mind control. There are many reports of Sarah Jacobson behaving erratically; last seen in the company of the perpetrator. Rumours also say they have been consorting with the Elvi.\'94\
After an extended series of gasps among the press, another journo asked, \'93Isn\'92t mind control an element in the Scarlet Shower Surgeon serial killings?\'94\
Alexander shook his head and crossed his arms, but the Commissioner launched anyway: \'93We know the Scarlet Shower Surgeon struck on the night of the Stickett Inn bombing, where we\'92ve established Chantara was present, so it\'92s reasonable to pin the not-for-profit terrorist for those crimes as well.\'94\
A guttural roar escaped Halo: anger, outrage, maybe something worse. He snarled and hurled his tablet at a screen, which woke its Labrador app from background processing. Whether by bug or by a sudden leap in artificial prescience, it scanned the Commissioner\'92s image and notified Halo, with cool certainty, that the man was already dead.
